{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20","id":966799,"title":"[Hunter the Reckoning] Your Own H20!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-10T09:53:14-07:00","id":966799,"title":"[Hunter the Reckoning] Your Own H20!","content":"What do you recommend for making your own V20 version of HtR. What books would you use? Rules? Stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T11:58:46-07:00","id":966853,"title":"","content":"1) Ability clean up, though that's par for course for the X20 books so far (sort of). For example, why do hunters need Alertness, Awareness, and Intuition? They're all just Perception + X Talents.<br /> <br /> 2) Change the way Virtues interact with Derangements. It's just too unwieldy at high levels, and doesn't really help illustrate the idea of the Hunt slowly driving the Imbued mad. Instead it's just sane one day, nut job the next, and super extra special ultra crazy the next. Not to pull too much from the CofD but in CofD 1e, Derangements had two levels. It wouldn't be hard to do something similar with this. Instead of four Derangements for hitting Virtue 10, one Derangement that keeps getting worse (or a mix of levels with multiples linked to how many different Edge Paths you've gone with so taking all three Paths gives you more quirks but easier to manage, but one Path gives you one clear derangement that gets really bad).<br /> <br /> 3) Move the Virtue/Edge math so 5s are achievable (at least the Core and Creedbook ones), which really aren't worth the hoops as written. Have a final &quot;capstone&quot; Edge level that you do the whole angel/demon/extremist deal to get.<br /> <br /> 4) Expand the Creedbook Conviction rewards so that Conviction isn't quite such a slog to increase. It's too easy with the base rules to end up with a wash most scenes.<br /> <br /> 5) Have the XP optional rules from the PG, but make them so there's some respect to the idea of only ever getting a small set of Edges instead of being able to buy all of them as that system allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:52:32-07:00","id":967021,"title":"","content":"Give them the 13/9/5 spread for Abilities as per the chargen in Hunter's Hunted 2.<br /> <br /> Give a bonus in an Attribute, depending on Creed.<br /> <br /> Provide more utilitarian Edge effects.<br /> <br /> Introduce the concept of aggravated damage and have Cleave deal it, so we can all stop writing around the concept.<br /> <br /> Introduce fuel stats for stripped-down monster stats, so that you don't deal with crazy-high Willpower ratings.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to the official one, though. The end of &quot;screw you, hippie!&quot; design means that you can finally have what will no doubt be an amusing first interaction between an imbued and a Mokole (they didn't get a writeup in Moonstruck). Just a few more years....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T02:49:51-07:00","id":967245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=967021#post967021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Introduce the concept of aggravated damage and have Cleave deal it, so we can all stop writing around the concept.<br /> <br /> Introduce fuel stats for stripped-down monster stats, so that you don't deal with crazy-high Willpower ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these were done in supplements (well, having Cleave do agg automatically wasn't, but addressing the idea was) already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:59:41-07:00","id":967313,"title":"","content":"Which suppliments heavy arms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:36:31-07:00","id":967333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=967021#post967021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Introduce the concept of aggravated damage and have Cleave deal it, so we can all stop writing around the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:53:00-07:00","id":967342,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms and Saur Ops both pretty much covered every update I'd want out of H20, so I think the only thing I'd add is a streamlining of the merits and flaws. There's a number of them that seem to have been copy/pasted from the other corebooks but which don't really interact well with the feel of Reckoning, and while the abundance of &quot;mundane&quot; merits and flaws relating to their every day life are a great addition they can get a little specific and nitpicky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:23:07-07:00","id":967392,"title":"","content":"Are there plans to do a 20th anniversary edition? To the best of my knowledge for WoD 4e (the new thing with Paradox) it's just Mage, Vampire, and Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:55:09-07:00","id":967607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=967313#post967313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which suppliments heavy arms?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Players Guide, the ST Handbook, the ST Companion, and the individual monster books cover those topics IIRC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=967392#post967392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there plans to do a 20th anniversary edition? To the best of my knowledge for WoD 4e (the new thing with Paradox) it's just Mage, Vampire, and Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's been no announcement of H20, but it is different from the One WoD aka WoD 5e (it's 5e now, not 4e) anyway. It's unclear if we'll see any 20th books for games after the original five that are already done/started for a number of reasons (one of which is WW wanted to have the focus on their new 5e is going to mean they'll going to want to slow down/stop the 20th books at some point).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T11:39:39-07:00","id":977272,"title":"","content":"Id be more interested in seeing the Evolution, from &quot;Spontaneous grabbing a random makeshift weapon&quot;&quot; to &quot;Organized Cult/Militia&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:17:23-07:00","id":977290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=977272#post977272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Id be more interested in seeing the Evolution, from &quot;Spontaneous grabbing a random makeshift weapon&quot;&quot; to &quot;Organized Cult/Militia&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>as for the spontenous grabbing..wel...the idea is that powers work because of urge, need and improvisation.. and organized cult? nah, the whole deal of the hunter's is them being average joe's. the idea of Organized Hunter's would make them Too overpowered. i love the fact of them being random strangers who barely know what a fuck is going on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:54:59-07:00","id":977319,"title":"","content":"Agreed, the everyman quality of Reckoning is what keeps it consistently compelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T13:57:10-07:00","id":977372,"title":"","content":"I know that, but seeing how they evolved, would be equally compelling.<br /> <br /> Failure to organize and form into a Cult/Militia, suggests the Monsters are winning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:18:03-07:00","id":977391,"title":"","content":"I don't think organized Hunters should be off the table, there's a whole original supplement in the game line about it.<br /> <br /> Hunters as also from the get go, starting to organize via things like Hunter-net.org.<br /> <br /> The key thing for H20 to include is having organization building from the ground up as a mode of play, rather than having preexisting Imbued large scale organizations plopped in the setting for the Imbued to join. Utopia and Holy War are already in the game line about this sort of thing (both the PCs doing it, or the PCs encountering someone else that already has gotten the ball rolling).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:52:37-07:00","id":977412,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's something quite compelling about a group developing their own cell with shared Backgrounds, a shared base, a network to communicate, etc. It creates an excellent basis for group storytelling too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T20:38:34-07:00","id":977572,"title":"","content":"Hurmm, maybe there could be an organization within the hunters. but everyone has its suspicious about them (maybe a public faction/guerilla leaded by Wayward's could tip some imbued off) or some Mysterious Groups too paranoid to trust any outsiders &quot;Knowing&quot; that The Enemy is inside hunter net.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T02:27:24-07:00","id":977668,"title":"","content":"I would add factions from &quot;Hunter: the Vigil&quot; and the imbued hunters wouldn't be &quot;newcomers&quot; but &quot;veterans&quot;, from time ago with the demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:05:44-07:00","id":977740,"title":"","content":"I'd honestly have preferred it if Imbued were far more of a rarity and largely ignorant of one another- no Hunter-Net or other organizing forces- although given the de-emphasis on the apocalyptic metaplot I'm not even sure how well Hunter fits thematically anymore- with the book characterizing them as a subset (suitable for PCs given that they don't get as trivially trashed by readily available supernatural powers as ordinary folk) of the wider, disparate range of independent* hunter archetypes in existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> *The mere existence of formal institutions like the Society of Leopold and Project Twilight are basically the failure of the Masquerade/Veil incarnate- it's not clear on how we're supposed to take the whole &quot;conceal yourself from mortals&quot; paradigm seriously when there have been institutionalized hunters for decades or even centuries. How has this not caused it all to come crashing down? Can you imagine the Congressional discussion on a bill allocating funding and authority for something like SAD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 09-28-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T08:57:00-07:00","id":977790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=977668#post977668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add factions from &quot;Hunter: the Vigil&quot; and the imbued hunters wouldn't be &quot;newcomers&quot; but &quot;veterans&quot;, from time ago with the demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't really appropriate to anything that's going to be sold as, &quot;Hunter: the Reckoning 20th Anniversary Edition.&quot;<br /> <br /> H20 shouldn't be scared of changing some things; esp. in terms of updating the setting to 20?? and addressing mechanical stuff that didn't get hammered out because it only had one regular edition. But it shouldn't be HtV in the WoD, and it shouldn't lose the core premise of the original line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=977740#post977740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd honestly have preferred it if Imbued were far more of a rarity and largely ignorant of one another- no Hunter-Net or other organizing forces- although given the de-emphasis on the apocalyptic metaplot I'm not even sure how well Hunter fits thematically anymore- with the book characterizing them as a subset (suitable for PCs given that they don't get as trivially trashed by readily available supernatural powers as ordinary folk) of the wider, disparate range of independent* hunter archetypes in existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, we're talking about H20, not &quot;WoD Hunters featuring all sorts of things pllus the Imbued.&quot; We already have Hunters Hunted II for V20.<br /> <br /> The 'de-emphasis&quot; on the metaplot should be leveraged, but towards adjusting to different kinds of play that would be valid to the HtR experience, such as &quot;the Imbued did crop up ~2000 during the massive supernatural upheavals of the time, and have had 15 years to become more than just random people running around bumping through the dark,&quot; all the way to, &quot;shift the creation of the Imbued to a bit before [Current Time] where it's more the original premise updated to now.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:53:16-07:00","id":977815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=977740#post977740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd honestly have preferred it if Imbued were far more of a rarity and largely ignorant of one another- no Hunter-Net or other organizing forces- although given the de-emphasis on the apocalyptic metaplot I'm not even sure how well Hunter fits thematically anymore- with the book characterizing them as a subset (suitable for PCs given that they don't get as trivially trashed by readily available supernatural powers as ordinary folk) of the wider, disparate range of independent* hunter archetypes in existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> *The mere existence of formal institutions like the Society of Leopold and Project Twilight are basically the failure of the Masquerade/Veil incarnate- it's not clear on how we're supposed to take the whole &quot;conceal yourself from mortals&quot; paradigm seriously when there have been institutionalized hunters for decades or even centuries. How has this not caused it all to come crashing down? Can you imagine the Congressional discussion on a bill allocating funding and authority for something like SAD?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> SAD Has explicitly tried to keep things secret from the government.<br /> <br /> they know, that if the existence of the supernatural became public knowledge it would lead to riots on the street, mad witch hunts, and the destruction of all social institutions, thus they are forced to act as de facto allies to the very creatures they fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:14:22-07:00","id":977823,"title":"","content":"the problem of the hunters being Organized, its the fact that they would become too powerful. and the idea of the setting is &quot;How desperated are you?&quot;.<br /> now, what its possible is to have veteran hunter's from BEFORE the existance of hunter net, but they would be a rarity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:26:40-07:00","id":977829,"title":"","content":"Something which I think will prove interesting in the process of updating is the sense of impending Armageddon. Reckoning felt heavily tied into the Time of Judgement and all of its millenniarian retinue. There undercurrent of existential dread was always a big part of it, at least from my perspective. The idea that Imbuings were happening because something had gone very, very wrong and that your learning curve as a hunter was going to be steep because cataclysm was right around the corner. We're over that hump now though, and the other 20th lines are generally moving away from that metaplot angle, so I'm curious how Hunter is going to feel without that Sword of Damocles hanging over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T13:03:05-07:00","id":977919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=977823#post977823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the problem of the hunters being Organized, its the fact that they would become too powerful. and the idea of the setting is &quot;How desperated are you?&quot;.<br /> now, what its possible is to have veteran hunter's from BEFORE the existance of hunter net, but they would be a rarity</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how organization makes the Imbued too powerful. They're ages behind most of their organized foes. They don't grow significantly more powerful with access to each other.<br /> <br /> Again, Utopia explores the complications and difficulties Hunters trying to step up their game, and how it doesn't just make everything easier for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=977829#post977829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which I think will prove interesting in the process of updating is the sense of impending Armageddon. Reckoning felt heavily tied into the Time of Judgement and all of its millenniarian retinue. There undercurrent of existential dread was always a big part of it, at least from my perspective. The idea that Imbuings were happening because something had gone very, very wrong and that your learning curve as a hunter was going to be steep because cataclysm was right around the corner. We're over that hump now though, and the other 20th lines are generally moving away from that metaplot angle, so I'm curious how Hunter is going to feel without that Sword of Damocles hanging over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the &quot;20th lines are moving away from the metaplot&quot; thing is being rather exaggerated in this discussion.<br /> <br /> The 20th books are metaplot &quot;agnostic&quot; so they can be used at any point in the original metaplot and don't seek to advance it in any meaningful way.<br /> <br /> If H20 happens, it will focus on the point in the metaplot the game needs to because it doesn't have a 1e and 2e edition's metaplot to include.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:27:23-07:00","id":978141,"title":"","content":"Another Thing on SAD is in Project Twilight, most of the government seems to think their just experts in occult style crimes, like Cults and such.<br /> <br /> And giving grudging research into psychic phenomena &quot;Just to show the public were not closed minded&quot; <br /> <br /> Most of the FBI and government views them that way, not knowing how many supernaturals they've actually fought, why the SAD is NOT as well funded as they'd like to be.<br /> <br /> In X20 with the shakeup... all I can say is whoever wrote the section on them in Hunters Hunted II had a VENDETTA","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T14:12:28-07:00","id":980424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=977829#post977829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which I think will prove interesting in the process of updating is the sense of impending Armageddon. Reckoning felt heavily tied into the Time of Judgement and all of its millenniarian retinue. There undercurrent of existential dread was always a big part of it, at least from my perspective. The idea that Imbuings were happening because something had gone very, very wrong and that your learning curve as a hunter was going to be steep because cataclysm was right around the corner. We're over that hump now though, and the other 20th lines are generally moving away from that metaplot angle, so I'm curious how Hunter is going to feel without that Sword of Damocles hanging over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have Future Fates like M20, they might show a hunter society emboldened by an apparent averting of the End Times. <br /> <br /> Maybe the Messengers are Imbuing fewer people, and the hunters who remain aren't fighting the impossible tide of Armageddon any more but for sheer survival as they face complete annihilation. <br /> <br /> Maybe they learn that they've always existed throughout the ages, but that their numbers grow and peak in cycles, coinciding with rising tensions in the supernatural world (see Dark Ages: Inquisitor). Now is merely a trough in hunter creation, but there will be more, and the Imbued will rise again...<br /> <br /> Maybe everything is the same, but HunterNET has migrated to an app (or takes advantage of existing ones like BBM?) and recent riots around the world have been fronts for hunter activity. Maybe they're compiling X files and wearing Guy Fawkes masks, or else they're joining the winning side...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:10:35-07:00","id":980481,"title":"","content":"unless the game is written just like mage with the<br /> A) Hunters appear as a answer to the armageddon<br /> B) Imbueds have been around for many years but only now they are starting to find each other<br /> C ) yada yada yadda<br /> <br /> kind of thing, instead of a more &quot;One line&quot; scenario, the game book could offer multiple choices depending on who is running the game","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T22:42:30-07:00","id":980588,"title":"","content":"One argument against the 'more organized' idea is that these are very dangerous times, politically, for anything that even resembles a terrorist network. And an organized Imbued group definitely does - and without the supernatural powers and entrenched power structures to divert attention that other groups possess.<br /> <br /> An organized group of armed extremists with cells worldwide, actively involved in regular and repeated acts of violence, arson, homicides, money laundering, kidnapping, and gun running? We're talking international anti-terror task forces, the FBI's <i>normal</i> elements getting involved (and SAD can only protect so many Imbued, when they're even inclined to do so), the CIA. That's without the potential for them being mistaken for a hate group and drawing the ire of the SPLC etc. Widespread organization for the Imbued may actually be self-defeating, because it will bring them to too much light too early. That could be a neat game to play in, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:17:16-07:00","id":980598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=980588#post980588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One argument against the 'more organized' idea is that these are very dangerous times, politically, for anything that even resembles a terrorist network. And an organized Imbued group definitely does - and without the supernatural powers and entrenched power structures to divert attention that other groups possess.<br /> <br /> An organized group of armed extremists with cells worldwide, actively involved in regular and repeated acts of violence, arson, homicides, money laundering, kidnapping, and gun running? We're talking international anti-terror task forces, the FBI's <i>normal</i> elements getting involved (and SAD can only protect so many Imbued, when they're even inclined to do so), the CIA. That's without the potential for them being mistaken for a hate group and drawing the ire of the SPLC etc. Widespread organization for the Imbued may actually be self-defeating, because it will bring them to too much light too early. That could be a neat game to play in, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the government organisations that hunt them down are guided by the Technocracy and vampires...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T03:16:02-07:00","id":982623,"title":"","content":"I've always felt like extended organizational/communication networks and long-term planning really undermined the sense of grit and desperation inherent to the concept of something like Hunter. Honestly I'd prefer it if there weren't anything like HunterNet at all- Imbued Hunters as largely isolated beyond whatever small groups coalesce together stochastically, without any sort of wider conspiracy that parallels the things they fight. If you can already orchestrate elaborate facades to conceal your offensives you lose the coherent sense of being an underdog against the monsters lurking in the shadows, thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:51:32-07:00","id":982720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=982623#post982623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always felt like extended organizational/communication networks and long-term planning really undermined the sense of grit and desperation inherent to the concept of something like Hunter. Honestly I'd prefer it if there weren't anything like HunterNet at all- Imbued Hunters as largely isolated beyond whatever small groups coalesce together stochastically, without any sort of wider conspiracy that parallels the things they fight. If you can already orchestrate elaborate facades to conceal your offensives you lose the coherent sense of being an underdog against the monsters lurking in the shadows, thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd need to respin the Vision creeds for that, though, since they're all about getting everyone together and organized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:10:27-07:00","id":982920,"title":"","content":"Balancing the desperation with organizations really isn't that hard: the Hunters have to build them. They don't exist already. Hunter-net.org is a start, but it's a seed that's just starting to grow. Any other larger organized Imbued groups presented in the game are still figuring out how to organize their members; let alone expand.<br /> <br /> Building up an organization is supposed to be part of the game (as was just noted, that's one of the big things for Visionaries), and building up one from scratch in the &quot;now&quot; of the setting is never going to rival the old conspiracies like the Camarilla or the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T04:25:21-07:00","id":984346,"title":"","content":"I'm confused, what's the difference between Hunters Hunted and Hunter the Reckoning? Because I thought that Hunters Hunted II covered plenty of stuff for a 20th anniversary game?<br /> <br /> Edit: Note that I only have Hunters Hunted II.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:41:10-07:00","id":984392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=984346#post984346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused, what's the difference between Hunters Hunted and Hunter the Reckoning? Because I thought that Hunters Hunted II covered plenty of stuff for a 20th anniversary game?<br /> <br /> Edit: Note that I only have Hunters Hunted II.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter: the Reckoning is its own game line and major splat within the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunter:_The_Reckoning\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Hunter_The_Reckoning_%28cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunter:_The_Reckoning\" target=\"_blank\"> Hunter: The Reckoning - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunter:_The_Reckoning\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunter:_The_Reckoning </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T07:59:55-07:00","id":984400,"title":"","content":"Hunter the Reckoning 20, an idea? <br /> <br /> introduce a new creed or two for anniversary edition.<br /> <br /> To mark the reckoning Gearing up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T13:30:06-07:00","id":984578,"title":"","content":"What would more Creed accomplish? There's 7 base Creeds, two Creeds that default to NPC status because of difficulty of use as PCs, and each Creed has three major philosophic groups detailed in their Creedbooks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:39:50-07:00","id":984893,"title":"","content":"The existing nine Creeds pretty much cover our bases, especially as each one seems to me to represent a primary Virtue and a secondary Virtue.<br /> <br /> Zeal + Mercy = Defender<br /> Zeal + Vision = Judge<br /> Zeal + Zeal = Avenger<br /> <br /> Mercy + Mercy = Innocent<br /> Mercy + Vision = Redeemer<br /> Mercy + Zeal = Martyr<br /> <br /> Vision + Mercy = Visionary<br /> Vision + Vision = Hermit<br /> Vision + Zeal = Wayward<br /> <br /> You'd need to introduce another Virtue to really expand the Creeds, which would entail a fairly major overhaul of core mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:48:00-07:00","id":984900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=984893#post984893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existing nine Creeds pretty much cover our bases, especially as each one seems to me to represent a primary Virtue and a secondary Virtue.<br /> <br /> Zeal + Mercy = Defender<br /> Zeal + Vision = Judge<br /> Zeal + Zeal = Avenger<br /> <br /> Mercy + Mercy = Innocent<br /> Mercy + Vision = Redeemer<br /> Mercy + Zeal = Martyr<br /> <br /> Vision + Mercy = Visionary<br /> Vision + Vision = Hermit<br /> Vision + Zeal = Wayward<br /> <br /> You'd need to introduce another Virtue to really expand the Creeds, which would entail a fairly major overhaul of core mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that way of looking at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T09:07:14-07:00","id":984908,"title":"","content":"H20 could revisit Hermits and Waywards with options to make them more functional as PCs to round out the numbers.<br /> <br /> It could also open up their Edge Paths (and give them a second set like the rest).<br /> <br /> One thing this does address in the rules is that unless you want to go down the Hermit/Wayward rabbit holes, Vision has a third of the Edges as Mercy and Zeal, making characters that take Vision feel very &quot;samey.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T09:48:08-07:00","id":984921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=984893#post984893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existing nine Creeds pretty much cover our bases, especially as each one seems to me to represent a primary Virtue and a secondary Virtue.<br /> <br /> Zeal + Mercy = Defender<br /> Zeal + Vision = Judge<br /> Zeal + Zeal = Avenger<br /> <br /> Mercy + Mercy = Innocent<br /> Mercy + Vision = Redeemer<br /> Mercy + Zeal = Martyr<br /> <br /> Vision + Mercy = Visionary<br /> Vision + Vision = Hermit<br /> Vision + Zeal = Wayward<br /> <br /> You'd need to introduce another Virtue to really expand the Creeds, which would entail a fairly major overhaul of core mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. I've always thought Innocents were Mercy + Vision, Redeemers were Mercy + Mercy, Hermits were Vision + Mercy, and Visionaries were Vision + Vision, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:24:34-07:00","id":984997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=984908#post984908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">H20 could revisit Hermits and Waywards with options to make them more functional as PCs to round out the numbers.<br /> <br /> It could also open up their Edge Paths (and give them a second set like the rest).<br /> <br /> One thing this does address in the rules is that unless you want to go down the Hermit/Wayward rabbit holes, Vision has a third of the Edges as Mercy and Zeal, making characters that take Vision feel very &quot;samey.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I've played several Visionaries and it feels like you pretty much have to double dip in one of the other Virtues to pad them out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=984921#post984921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mm. I've always thought Innocents were Mercy + Vision, Redeemers were Mercy + Mercy, Hermits were Vision + Mercy, and Visionaries were Vision + Vision, myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's not any kind of exact schema. I've gone back and forth on Innocents and Redeemers, though I err on calling Redeemers the &quot;Mercy + Vision&quot; Creed by dint of several of their Edges having a reflective bent to them. By the same token I tend to call Hermits the &quot;Double Vision&quot; Creed because they seem to be overwhelmed with direct info dumps from the Messengers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:35:32-07:00","id":985035,"title":"","content":"To me it was less of a problem for Visionaries (since the game heavily incentivizes having your Creed Edges be the only ones you use for your primal Virtue points), but for any of the other Creeds that wanted to branch into Vision because they can only go down the Vision Edge path.<br /> <br /> The Vision Edges also kinda redundant for a lot of characters to have. A lot of the Mercy and Zeal Edges have some low level options that it's kinda useful to have a bunch of characters with (Bluster, Cleave, Impact, Ward/Rejuvenate, the non-Vision Second Sight boosters, etc.). So even if there's a lot of overlap it doesn't feel weird because the more the merrier with those (though the different problem of everyone wanting them because of the sheer utility factor).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:40:38-07:00","id":985041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/966799-hunter-the-reckoning-your-own-h20?p=984997#post984997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it's not any kind of exact schema. I've gone back and forth on Innocents and Redeemers, though I err on calling Redeemers the &quot;Mercy + Vision&quot; Creed by dint of several of their Edges having a reflective bent to them. By the same token I tend to call Hermits the &quot;Double Vision&quot; Creed because they seem to be overwhelmed with direct info dumps from the Messengers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've gone by approach to the hunt. Innocents are about keeping an open mind about monsters, serving as a group's conscience, questioning whether they're doing the right thing. Redeemers, meanwhile, focus on redemption and healing.<br /> <br /> Visionaries are big-picture thinkers, putting together theories, organising the imbued; I don't really see any particular inclination towards Mercy in them. Trouble is, there's not much Mercy in the Hermits, either, at least as the Virtue's usually portrayed. At a stretch, their focus on communication, on sending and receiving information and ideas, could point Mercy-wards, given the Virtue's focus on connection and empathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}